    {
      "id": "ACP-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Every positive-degree cocycle on the free lattice has a finite cup decomposition",
      "anchor": "inputs-additive-prism",
      "statement": "For any j≥1 and any invariant closed c in the real homogeneous complex of a finite-rank free abelian group, c is exactly a finite real linear combination of ordered j-fold cups plus δe for an invariant (j−1)-cochain e.",
      "hypotheses": "The induction splits P=ℤ×G by prepending a coordinate and uses the full homogeneous tuple complex. A finite integral basis identifies the translation lattice with such a coordinate lattice.",
      "definitions": [
        "ι(g)=(0,g), ρ(h,g)=g, ℓ(h,g)=h, ψ(h,g)=(−1,g).",
        "With U=ρ*ι*c, use b=ι*Kψ(U−c), retaining the prism of U. The restricted prism of ℓ∪ρ*b is −b.",
        "For R=c−U−ℓ∪ρ*b the primitive starts from x=KιρR with δx=−R. The finite signed sum W corrects x to an invariant primitive −x+δW in degrees at least two.",
        "The existence statement does not specify a basis of cohomology or uniqueness of the expression."
      ],
